# A CANDIDATE: PAGING AS THE ENGINE'S DEFAULT (operator, 2026-11-25, relayed
# by the architecture session: "Set the new paging mode as the default in the
# engine"). d531d5d804f1's series, line for line, then:
#   0021  on SYCL a model pages by default: GGML_SYCL_BMG_VRAM_CHECK 0 and
#         GGML_SYCL_HOST_PINNED_MEM_2G 1 where upstream has 1 and 0. A
#         model's own file still decides for that model.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-page.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ANOTHER ENGINE: a build and every gate again, and two defaults carried
# against upstream's. Every encoder runs under buffers of 2 GiB at most: it
# must gate as d531d5d804f1 does, fingerprint for fingerprint, or it rolls
# back - where a buffer ends is not what is computed in it, and the gate is
# what says so.
# NOT BEFORE 0018's ROW HAS PASSED on the live engine (a refused pool commit
# answered by the same process): a default that pages before the refusal
# reaches the graph is the defect already seen. And the keeper's own default
# (`[models] make_room = "page"`) is merged only once THIS engine is the live
# one - docs/notes/room-on-the-card.md §3.
